# Personal values that must never reach a commit. Copy this file and fill in your own:
#
#     cp .pii-denylist.example .pii-denylist
#
# One value per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Matching is case-insensitive substring
# over every staged line, so entries must be specific enough not to fire on ordinary code — six characters is a
# sensible floor. A first name would match a variable; a house number plus street name would not.
#
# This is the layer that catches REPEATS with certainty. The semantic pass in scripts/pii-scan.mjs catches novel
# values it has never been told about. Both run from .githooks/pre-commit.
#
# Your real `.pii-denylist` is gitignored precisely because it is, by construction, a file of your own personal
# data. Never commit it, and never paste its contents into an issue, a PR, or a bug report.
#
# Fill in the values that appear in YOUR captures — the plugins you connect are the ones whose recordings you
# transcribe into fixtures, and those recordings carry your real account.

# Residence — street address, unit, postal code
# 1234 RUE DE L'EXEMPLE
# H1A 1A1

# Government and utility account identifiers — property roll number, dossier, policy, licence
# 00000000000000000000000
# 50-00000000

# Personal access codes and portal handles
# MYACCESSCODE

# Real email addresses and phone numbers used to sign in
# me@my-real-domain.com
# 514-555-0100

# Real account, customer, or host identifiers assigned to you by a service
# 000000000
